-- title:
--   Cusp-regular level-M' functions are integral over ℚ[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $M'$ be a positive integer and let $g \in \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ be a Laurent series lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,d\;j_q$ for the positive divisors $d$ of $M'$, where $j_q = q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{Num},\mathbb{Q}}$ is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Write $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and let `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images under `coeffEmb` of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`. The hypothesis is a regularity condition: for every place $P$ of this field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — that is, every valuation subring, distinct from the whole field, containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a principal ideal ring — if the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` determined by the coefficientwise image of $j_q$ has $\operatorname{ord}_P \ge 0$, then so does the element determined by the coefficientwise image of $g$; here $\operatorname{ord}_P$ is minus the logarithm of the adic valuation attached to the maximal ideal of the valuation ring. The conclusion is that $g$ is integral over the $\mathbb{Q}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{Q}[j_q]$ of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated by $j_q$, i.e. $g$ satisfies a monic polynomial with coefficients in $\mathbb{Q}[j_q]$. Thus regularity is imposed over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ while integrality is obtained over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the classical statement that a modular function of level $M'$ which is regular wherever $j$ is regular (that is, away from the cusps) is integral over $\mathbb{Q}[j]$, the places where $j$ is regular being exactly the valuation rings of the function field containing $j$. It feeds the chart-membership results for the full-level modular curve, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.inclusion_mem_chartAlgFin_of_mem_integers_of_cuspRegular_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.inclusion_mem_chartAlgFin_of_mem_integers_of_cuspRegular_descent) and its variants for levels two and three.
